Storage & Data Transfer

Storage Gateway: Hybrid cloud storage service with 3 types:

File Gateway: File interface to S3 using NFS/SMB
Tape Gateway: Virtual tape library interface for S3
FSX Gateway: Low-latency access to AWS FSx
Volume Gateway: Block storage volumes mountable as iSCSI devices


Data Transfer:

AWS Application Migration Service: Execution tool for migrating servers to EC2
AWS Application Discovery Service: Planning tool for migration projects
AWS Transfer Family: Managed file transfer for Amazon S3
AWS DataSync: Automated data transfer between on-premises and AWS storage
Snowmobile: For datasets of 10PB+ in a single location
Snowball Edge: For datasets less than 10PB or distributed across locations



Databases & Caching

Redis:

Multi-AZ, Read replicas, Persistent, Backup/restore, Data structures & key-value pairs


Memcache:

Sharding, Non-persistent, Serverless, Key-value pair, Multi-thread architecture


DynamoDB:

Query: Searches within specific partition key (efficient)
Scan: Searches through entire table (less efficient)



S3 & Content Delivery

S3 Access Control:

Object Ownership: Controls object ownership from other AWS accounts
Bucket Owner Preferred: Objects with bucket-owner-full-control ACL owned by bucket owner
Object Writer: Original writer remains object owner
ACLs Disabled: All objects owned by account, access via policies only
ACLs Enabled: Objects can be owned by other accounts, access via ACLs


Content Delivery:

Signed URLs: One URL per file for one-time access
Signed Cookies: One cookie for multiple files (premium content access)
Global Accelerator: Network service improving global application performance



AI & Machine Learning Services

Comprehend: Machine learning for text document analysis
Connect: Cloud-based contact center platform
Lex: Conversational AI for chatbots and voice assistants
Polly: Text-to-speech conversion
Recognition: ML-based identification of people/objects in images/videos
Transcribe: Speech-to-text conversion
Translate: Language translation

Monitoring & Management

CloudTrail:

Management Events: Records administrative actions
Data Events: Tracks resource-level operations
Insights: Detects unusual API activity patterns


CloudWatch:

CloudWatch Unified Agent: Collects metrics, logs, and traces
CloudWatch Logs Agent: Collects and streams log files
Data Sources: Elastic Beanstalk, ECS, Lambda, VPC Flow Logs, API Gateway, CloudTrail, EC2, Route 53


Management Tools:

AWS OpsWorks: Configuration management using Puppet/Chef
AWS Systems Manager: Secure management and patching solution
Parameter Store: Centralized storage for configuration data and secrets
AWS Config: Auditing and compliance recording
AWS Control Tower: Automated setup of secure multi-account environments



Security & Compliance

Network Security:

Security Groups: Stateful - return traffic automatically allowed
Network ACLs: Stateless - each packet evaluated independently
WAF Logs: Sent to CloudWatch Logs, S3, Kinesis Data Firehose


Identity & Access:

Service Control Policies (SCPs): Maximum permissions boundaries for organization
Guard Duty: Monitors for malicious activity
Active Directory: Microsoft directory service for authentication



Networking

VPC Connectivity:

VPC Peering: Connection between two VPCs using private IP addresses
VPC Sharing: Allows multiple accounts to create resources in shared subnets
Virtual Private Gateway: For private, encrypted on-premises communication
Internet Gateway: For VPC resources to communicate with public internet
Direct Connect: Physical dedicated private connection to AWS
VPN: Encrypted connection over public internet


VPC Endpoints:

Gateway Endpoints: For S3/DynamoDB using private IPs
Interface Endpoints: For endpoint services using Network Load Balancer
Gateway Load Balancer Endpoints: For virtual appliance fleets using private IPs


Direct Connect Interfaces:

Public VIF: Connect to public AWS endpoints using public IP
Private VIF: Connect to VPC resources using private IP
Transit VIF: Connect to multiple VPCs across regions via Transit Gateway


Load Balancing:

Application Load Balancer (ALB): Layer 7, HTTP/HTTPS traffic, content-based routing
Network Load Balancer (NLB): Layer 4, TCP/UDP/TLS traffic, extreme performance



Compute & Containers

EC2 Related:

EBS Snapshot: Point-in-time backup of EBS volume data
AMI: Complete backup of EC2 instance (OS, data, configurations)
Auto Scaling: Creates new scaling activity to replace unhealthy instances


Migration Strategies:

Rehosting: Application migration without major configuration changes
Replatforming: Application migration with AWS services integration



Message & Event Services

SQS:

Standard: Unlimited throughput, at-least-once delivery, best-effort ordering
FIFO: First-In-First-Out, exactly-once processing, limited throughput
Visibility Timeout: Prevents message duplication and race conditions


SNS: Push-based messaging to multiple receivers (pub/sub model)
Event Services:

EventBridge: Routes events to AWS services, schedules actions, archives events
EventBridge Pipes: Simplifies producer-consumer integration
EventBridge Scheduler: Manages millions of scheduled tasks
Step Functions: Orchestrates multiple AWS services into workflows



Analytics & Database

Analytics:

Amazon Athena: Interactive query service for S3 data using SQL
Kinesis Data Streams: Real-time custom processing with sub-second latency
Kinesis Firehose: Load streaming data into destinations with auto scaling


Database High Availability:

Aurora Global Database: For global applications with cross-region low latency
Aurora Read Replicas: For scaling read operations (asynchronous)
Aurora Multi-AZ: For high availability within a region (synchronous)



Cost Management

AWS Budgets: For proactive cost controls and alerts
Cost Explorer: For analyzing historical spending patterns

Miscellaneous

Route 53 Resolver: Resolves DNS queries in VPC and on-premises network
AWS Outposts: AWS infrastructure and services for on-premises locations
Host Affinity: Software licensing based on physical cores